2186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167161 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186305033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186305034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186305035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186305036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186305037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186459220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Laplace Transformed Solution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166932 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "bb88b85b-efa1-56db-8655-4b49703dda6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Laplace Transforms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186167890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167006 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "18df0fdd-60be-5a81-a0cd-e95103dfb1c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186164005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1069 "q-322280" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "17eee175-34bb-5ca1-9aad-a080088cd275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167159 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-1={X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{1}{s-1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+3=-(\\frac{1}{s-1})+3{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-3s+2}{(s-1)(s-3)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1061 590676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "648d1a99-8c25-5200-8b95-382792dca052" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167886 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186167982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1061 590677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "887d1a2a-3793-57e6-a390-bcc123897754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167887 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1061 590680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c39529f2-6303-5dd8-a113-cdaf40a5d673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1061 590683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa736c0f-1eaa-5601-a02e-62159a1f73b2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1061 590687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f663bde1-a39c-5d4d-83fd-15b833a5cbea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167890 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1064 "![](images/44/44a90d0fa61d3643848f01479706cca752a00914b99185da5b8739c5e1cab182.svg)\n\n**Step 1**. In the initial value problem above, we apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation.\n\nFirst, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{5{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=5L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+6L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+3=5{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-2{X}_{1}(s)+6{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\}$ and $X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.$\n\n**Step 2**. Now, solving the first equation for $X_1(s),$ we get\n\n$$\ns X_1(s) +  3 = 5 X_1(s)\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_1(s) = -\\dfrac{3}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for $X_2(s),$ we have\n\n$$\ns X_2(s) -  2 = -2\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{s-5}\\right) + 6 X_2(s) \n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nX_2(s) = \\dfrac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**. To find $x_1(t)$ and $x_2(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to $X_1(s)$ and $X_2(s){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{-\\frac{3}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{2s-4}{(s-5)(s-6)}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{8}{s-6}-\\frac{6}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\}-6{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{5t} \\\\ 8{e}^{6t}-6{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1065 14201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a475ed27-9529-52d2-85cb-9e8827c5b45e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167982 #edb/ref 1067 "A Worked Example" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1064 "In this topic, we'll learn how to use Laplace transforms to solve homogeneous systems like the one below.\n![](images/66/66eb9ce1b87b67ba550fc0b76493b775bf2b2e67be257b9fe9974db9d53cdffa.svg)\n\nThe process can be split into three steps.\n\n- **Step 1.** Apply the Laplace transform $\\mathcal{L}$ to both sides of each equation, to get a system with variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_1(t) \\right\\} \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s) = \\mathcal{L}\\left\\{  x_2(t) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Solve the obtained system for variables \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\n- **Step 3.** To find the initial variables\n\n$$\nx_1(t) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad x_2(t)\n$$\n\nsatisfying the original initial value problem, apply the inverse Laplace transform to \n\n$$\nX_1(s) \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad X_2(s).\n$$\n\nLet's see how this works in practice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1065 14610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "98573e3a-ebcd-565e-8de7-a83e3deb9d09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168031 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302842 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3db932f4-fae5-50c6-9f86-537475346704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303021 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c87bd0e-68f0-53c0-a1da-53a949f4133b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303219 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303219 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303219 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7b600c94-694f-5df9-8995-92f0759d4e67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303387 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303387 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303387 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "95d1ef6b-caf6-5764-bc12-294fa204246c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303464 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303464 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303464 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a3ce928a-a5a9-5225-8c9f-2f61190156c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303953 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{s+2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303953 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee8ef59c-2d4f-5cd8-bd73-bde62a85dcd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304299 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304299 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304299 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304299 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304299 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "518f0276-0f4b-5c49-a892-c180fc62763c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304304 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304304 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304304 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304304 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186302842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304304 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "51f9ccbb-98c5-5a7d-8a34-9b6a924b104f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304494 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304494 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304494 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304494 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304494 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9b95b873-f263-55a4-aa11-176bdc917560" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304540 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304540 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304540 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304540 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304540 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a99db976-4eb3-54c9-b026-70c5ab583549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304592 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304592 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304592 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304592 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304592 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bdcc71fe-ab2d-5096-8ba2-82ce4b706e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304720 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304720 #edb/ref 1077 "field-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304720 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186303021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304720 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ee8a77b9-f4f3-5da7-a356-159e03040e12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1069 "q-331918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}},\n$\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c4c84fb-7fb4-580a-bff4-417ed1ebd433" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304958 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-2{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=-2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-3L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get \n\n$$\ns{X}_{1}(s)-3=-2{X}_{1}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3}{s+2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s)$ gives\n\n$$\ns{X}_{2}(s)+4=-3(\\frac{3}{s+2})+4{X}_{2}(s)\\,⟹\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-4s-17}{(s-4)(s+2)}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-5{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$x(t)=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n$\\,\\,{e}^{6t}$\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "317fc248-dee8-522d-9f3a-ce7380dbab1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186305037 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{4}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}+4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{5}{s}-\\frac{4}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =5{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}-4{L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-6}\\} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6\\cdot t} \\\\  & =5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+4{e}^{6t} \\\\ 5-4{e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\